WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.800
Here's a line linguists love to quote.

2
00:00:02.850 --> 00:00:05.090
Time flies like an arrow.

3
00:00:05.140 --> 00:00:08.070
And then: fruit flies like a banana.

4
00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:09.290
Groan.

5
00:00:09.340 --> 00:00:13.530
But look again: the two halves
seem built exactly alike.

6
00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:17.020
So how can a line about
bananas be a grammar joke?

7
00:00:17.070 --> 00:00:19.990
In this mission, you'll
sort words into classes,

8
00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:23.550
open and closed, from
nouns to prepositions.

9
00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:26.810
You'll see how words group
into phrases round a head word,

10
00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:29.940
and ask where each phrase begins and ends.

11
00:00:29.990 --> 00:00:35.680
And you'll look inside words, at the tiny
parts that carry meaning all by themselves.

12
00:00:35.730 --> 00:00:39.640
Your mission: explain how
grammar makes the joke work.
